  "blurb": "The geometric alphabet of the Amazigh (Berber) languages: circles, lines and dots, 33 letters in the Moroccan standard.",
  "writeTip": "Tifinagh letters are built from straight lines, circles and dots. Draw lines top to bottom and left to right, and circles in one stroke from the top.",
  "audio": "ipa",
  "voice": "hi",
  "notes": [
    "Neo-Tifinagh for SquirrelGo Alphabets, in the IRCAM standard used for Amazigh (Berber) in Morocco. Romanization is the usual Latin spelling of Amazigh (ɣ for the gargled r, ɛ for the throat sound). eSpeak NG has no Amazigh voice, so the sounds are made from the IPA. Hints, groupings and articles are original."
  ],
